{"author":{"id":"038d65070aa747b6bc9d50939fa697ec871a40ed259db54429b255bbef2581d6"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1793388168,"nonce":"xKy2ebOKzZ+TpVEhBf1n+wgi5/4=","message":"MSB backend for the sandbox-provider interface: rayde_runner::Msb (native/runner/src/msb.rs). Reading the runner's real commands showed two gaps in the first draft, now in the trait: detach (the runner starts the session with exec --detach) and Source::Disk (it mounts disk.raw files with --mount-disk). Pure builders and parsers are unit-tested against the exact flags the runner uses; all 11 runner tests pass. Not run against a live MSB: msb_conforms is #[ignore] and needs a KVM host with MSB 0.7.11 plus RAYDE_MSB_CONFIG, creating and removing sandboxes, so the backend is untested live (the snapshot create command and read-only mount syntax in particular are unchecked). MSB 0.7.11 has no GPU flag; it does have --net-rule and --net-default, so an egress allowlist is probably expressible and is left unmapped. Next: run msb_conforms on the NUC, then move the runner's service code onto the trait.","files":null}]}